From ffdc15af9204f55b6e0554683504130f6801e77e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BEL <bel@H100-VM1.mzqbi1zdpcje1jsioelsqu3tog.rx.internal.cloudapp.net>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 10:49:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] [feat](kt-kernel): per-expert promote/evict for a
 three-tier expert store

release_expert() returns one expert's physical pages with madvise; load_expert()
stages a single expert straight from mmap'd safetensors. Together they let the
CPU store hold a bounded subset of experts, with the rest reachable only on
disk.

Per-expert BufferB allocations move from 64B to page alignment and a page
multiple, because MADV_DONTNEED only frees whole pages -- at 64B the first and
last page of each buffer are shared with a neighbour and cannot be released.

Origin: RunGLM experiment/expert-tiering-ssd.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
